[SPEAKER_01]: Is that what I learned?

679
00:59:10,711 --> 00:59:13,372
[SPEAKER_01]: Should I just stop this animal now, that's burning?

680
00:59:14,613 --> 00:59:15,513
[SPEAKER_01]: Or should I contain it?

681
00:59:17,743 --> 00:59:19,203
[SPEAKER_01]: Should I not follow along the lines?

682
00:59:19,743 --> 00:59:25,285
[SPEAKER_01]: Or should I just completely, as I said, choke it, asphyxiate it, get rid of it, replace it with a different state of mind?

683
00:59:26,605 --> 00:59:28,445
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, oh, but then I'm still acting out of the animal.

684
00:59:29,305 --> 00:59:41,408
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the main reason people keep falling into these patterns of, like, loops and vicious cycles and not able to... it's because they never address the real thing, which is the actual state of mind right there and then.

685
00:59:42,276 --> 00:59:43,437
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, they know it, obviously.

686
00:59:43,457 --> 00:59:44,237
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot know it.

687
00:59:44,257 --> 00:59:44,877
[SPEAKER_01]: You're feeling it.

688
00:59:45,277 --> 00:59:54,221
[SPEAKER_01]: But they go about it in every possible way, except the way of, hold on, how about I keep looking at you, instead of what you are offering me to look at.

689
00:59:56,902 --> 01:00:02,505
[SPEAKER_01]: And even if it's rooted in the same aversion, it's less inaccurate.

690
01:00:03,589 --> 01:00:20,963
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, going along the lines, which means they're going to be less desire, eh... eh... fettering you, less kind of involvement, which, in return, is going to make things clearer, which, in return, is going to make it next time even less inaccurate, and less inaccurate to the point of you'll be seeing it accurately, right through.

691
01:00:23,545 --> 01:00:28,629
[SPEAKER_01]: But it needs to be an active effort, and in this case, as I said, I mean, it's always an active effort.

692
01:00:28,709 --> 01:00:30,791
[SPEAKER_01]: Trying to concentrate away, it's an active effort.

693
01:00:30,971 --> 01:00:32,032
[SPEAKER_01]: It just falls flat.

694
01:00:33,137 --> 01:00:36,598
[SPEAKER_01]: You concentrate away, but then, five seconds later, the mind is still same.

695
01:00:38,198 --> 01:00:38,618
[SPEAKER_01]: Spiral.

696
01:00:39,218 --> 01:00:42,919
[SPEAKER_01]: The only time it stops, it's after four, five, six hours have passed.

697
01:00:43,259 --> 01:00:43,679
[SPEAKER_01]: Hopefully.

698
01:00:43,779 --> 01:00:44,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes not even then.

699
01:00:44,699 --> 01:00:46,360
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes three or four days, it still comes back.

700
01:00:47,540 --> 01:00:57,682
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you realize, oh, okay, basically, I am making the effort either way, in trying to get rid of it, trying to concentrate away from it.

701
01:00:58,042 --> 01:01:01,043
[SPEAKER_01]: How about, instead, I think about the real source of the issue here?

702
01:01:04,135 --> 01:01:04,856
[SPEAKER_01]: Reflect on it.

703
01:01:05,756 --> 01:01:06,997
[SPEAKER_01]: Ask questions about it.

704
01:01:07,758 --> 01:01:10,740
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything, just don't go along the offered lines of thought.

705
01:01:10,960 --> 01:01:11,301
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

706
01:01:12,802 --> 01:01:14,463
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, do I need to get rid of it?

707
01:01:14,563 --> 01:01:14,723
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

708
01:01:15,304 --> 01:01:16,485
[SPEAKER_01]: So, why am I trying to get rid of it?

709
01:01:16,645 --> 01:01:19,207
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I don't know, because I forgot that I don't have to get rid of it.

710
01:01:20,748 --> 01:01:25,151
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what if this state of mind stays for the rest of the day, but me not feeling it?

711
01:01:26,533 --> 01:01:27,413
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to do anything.

712
01:01:29,255 --> 01:01:31,697
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no right thing I could have said or I should have said.

713
01:01:32,778 --> 01:01:41,644
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that is fueled by the pain that the burning mind puts on you and you take for granted as something that I must deal with.

714
01:01:43,986 --> 01:01:55,713
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you overlook the level where you can deal with it and you think that dealing with it is our practice, my communication skills or something, so that this will be prevented in the future.

715
01:01:55,973 --> 01:01:57,675
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like you're still not dealing with it here and now.

716
01:01:58,545 --> 01:01:59,647
[SPEAKER_01]: You're addressing the future.

717
01:02:00,268 --> 01:02:04,314
[SPEAKER_01]: The phenomenon that pertains to the future, that is basis for desire and lust, as we just described.

718
01:02:04,734 --> 01:02:05,596
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what you're addressing.

719
01:02:05,616 --> 01:02:07,098
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not addressing desire and lust right now.

720
01:02:09,621 --> 01:02:17,927
[SPEAKER_01]: So, instead of falling into the trap, or when you fall into a trap and you recognize, you go like, oh, hold on, I have fallen into a trap, the burning mind pushed me into it, I didn't see it.

721
01:02:18,427 --> 01:02:19,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it still burning?

722
01:02:19,127 --> 01:02:19,508
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

723
01:02:19,548 --> 01:02:20,248
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it still unpleasant?

724
01:02:20,288 --> 01:02:20,468
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

725
01:02:21,109 --> 01:02:22,270
[SPEAKER_01]: Do I need to do anything about it?

726
01:02:23,050 --> 01:02:25,652
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I have a strong urge, but I don't have to do anything about it.

727
01:02:25,692 --> 01:02:29,154
[SPEAKER_01]: How about I make the effort of not doing anything about it, but not losing the sight of it either?

728
01:02:30,355 --> 01:02:36,279
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is already a form of doing something about it, just not on your own terms, not on the terms that are infused with lust and

729
01:02:39,163 --> 01:02:41,544
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can use the same momentum against the mind.

730
01:02:42,164 --> 01:02:58,849
[SPEAKER_01]: Instead of thinking the content that it offers, you think about the state of mind, the pressure, the unpleasantness of it, how unbeneficial it is to not have it trained, when something so trivial can disrupt it so much.

731
01:02:59,469 --> 01:03:01,050
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, oh, no, you are the problem.

732
01:03:01,866 --> 01:03:11,671
[SPEAKER_01]: Not the colleague, not what I said, not what I should have said, not now, not me refusing to think with what you want me to think, and then mind tries to pressure.

733
01:03:11,711 --> 01:03:12,572
[SPEAKER_01]: None of that's the problem.

734
01:03:12,652 --> 01:03:13,312
[SPEAKER_01]: You are the problem.

735
01:03:13,432 --> 01:03:18,995
[SPEAKER_01]: You're the problem that you're still capable of such upset, of such lust, of such desire, of such force.

736
01:03:19,875 --> 01:03:23,097
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the problem, and I need to keep an eye on it, because that's how I begin taming it.

737
01:03:24,688 --> 01:03:30,813
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, for as long as the momentum lasts, for as long... that long you use the momentum to think about the mind that's pushing into that momentum.

738
01:03:30,933 --> 01:03:35,817
[SPEAKER_01]: That's really... again, it's not an abstract thing, because it's going to be felt very much so.

739
01:03:35,877 --> 01:03:36,577
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, where's my mind?

740
01:03:36,857 --> 01:03:37,598
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is this animal?

741
01:03:37,978 --> 01:03:39,259
[SPEAKER_01]: It's right there where that pain is.

742
01:03:39,399 --> 01:03:43,543
[SPEAKER_01]: That is what the mind is.

743
01:03:43,583 --> 01:03:46,365
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like, oh, this pain is the mind.

744
01:03:47,790 --> 01:03:54,372
[SPEAKER_01]: Here and now, in practical terms, don't get all technical, the practical terms, it's what the mind is.

745
01:03:54,412 --> 01:03:56,832
[SPEAKER_01]: It's what stands for the mind most accurately there and then.

746
01:03:57,852 --> 01:04:02,413
[SPEAKER_01]: Affected with aversion, affected with lust, with all the implications that it has.

747
01:04:03,094 --> 01:04:04,814
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, aha, so you are the problem.

748
01:04:10,635 --> 01:04:11,415
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't get rid of it.

749
01:04:11,876 --> 01:04:13,716
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't just remove the mind, not have it.

750
01:04:15,617 --> 01:04:23,139
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, if you never read the suttas or listened to our talks, you would say, I don't really know what to do, but you heard so many times, so you know what to do.

751
01:04:23,159 --> 01:04:24,400
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you have the information.

752
01:04:25,680 --> 01:04:30,221
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, you are the problem, I shall not fuel it, but I shall not try to deny you either.

753
01:04:30,381 --> 01:04:31,962
[SPEAKER_01]: I will recognize you as the problem.

754
01:04:33,462 --> 01:04:35,723
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, when you are not a problem, I will recognize you as not a problem.

755
01:04:37,805 --> 01:04:38,425
[SPEAKER_01]: And then stay with it.

756
01:04:38,505 --> 01:04:42,988
[SPEAKER_01]: And whenever it comes up, the trigger or whatever, it's like, it's the mind that's the trigger.

757
01:04:43,869 --> 01:04:49,712
[SPEAKER_01]: Not the specific thoughts that feels like prompted you and made you feel this or made you feel that.

758
01:04:49,732 --> 01:04:49,953
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no.

759
01:04:50,013 --> 01:04:50,593
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the animal.

760
01:04:51,514 --> 01:04:55,136
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the animal still being touchy, still being twitchy, still being liable to these things.

761
01:04:55,216 --> 01:05:03,261
[SPEAKER_01]: So, by seeing the animal, you already kind of dealt with 50% of the problem, which is not seeing the animal and falling into the loops.

762
01:05:04,794 --> 01:05:06,034
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not going to be perfect, as I said.

763
01:05:06,054 --> 01:05:07,475
[SPEAKER_01]: You're going to fall into luce and catch yourself.

764
01:05:07,795 --> 01:05:09,875
[SPEAKER_01]: But whenever you catch yourself, you don't double down.

765
01:05:10,195 --> 01:05:14,116
[SPEAKER_01]: I must try harder to concentrate away from the whole thing and shut my mind.

766
01:05:14,776 --> 01:05:14,976
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

767
01:05:15,397 --> 01:05:21,418
[SPEAKER_01]: I must try harder to not lose the corner of my eye from the pressuring problem here and now, which is the state of citta.

768
01:05:22,538 --> 01:05:23,338
[SPEAKER_01]: The soul problem.

769
01:05:23,458 --> 01:05:23,699
[SPEAKER_01]: Always.

770
01:05:23,719 --> 01:05:25,379
[SPEAKER_01]: There was never any other problem in your life.

771
01:05:26,371 --> 01:05:28,934
[SPEAKER_01]: It was always the state of citta, affected with only three things.

772
01:05:29,175 --> 01:05:30,977
[SPEAKER_01]: Greed, aversion or distraction.

773
01:05:31,498 --> 01:05:32,279
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no fourth.

774
01:05:32,960 --> 01:05:35,303
[SPEAKER_01]: Just these three things, always on that level.

775
01:05:35,383 --> 01:05:38,407
[SPEAKER_01]: And I always keep saying that, because it always ties into everything.

776
01:05:38,427 --> 01:05:43,274
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like that sutta when... when they asked the Buddha, oh, you said dhamma is directly visible here and now.

777
01:05:43,394 --> 01:05:44,115
[SPEAKER_01]: How is it so?

778
01:05:45,139 --> 01:05:53,183
[SPEAKER_01]: And you would think, oh, because you concentrate on a subatomic particle of the, you know, multitude of your insight, of some secret hidden dimensions.

779
01:05:53,203 --> 01:05:53,764
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, no.

780
01:05:54,064 --> 01:05:59,547
[SPEAKER_01]: Dhamma is visible, here and now, when you know mind of lust as mind of lust.

781
01:06:00,227 --> 01:06:05,550
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, when you have not fallen into a trap, or follow along the lines, got distracted, got lost, or acted out, even worse.

782
01:06:06,391 --> 01:06:09,832
[SPEAKER_01]: When you know mind of aversion as mind of aversion, mind of distraction, mind of distraction.

783
01:06:11,173 --> 01:06:14,335
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, when you know the state of mind for what it is, when you see it, aha, I see you.

784
01:06:16,122 --> 01:06:17,343
[SPEAKER_01]: That's... you are the issue.

785
01:06:18,624 --> 01:06:23,166
[SPEAKER_01]: You reacting to this, this way, that way, sometimes like this... That's... you are the problem.

786
01:06:23,627 --> 01:06:29,730
[SPEAKER_01]: Your lack of tameness, lack of... your desires, your dependence on desires, you are the problem.

787
01:06:30,391 --> 01:06:34,113
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how you see the dhamma, here and now, directly visible.

788
01:06:34,133 --> 01:06:37,355
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if you had no instruction in dhamma whatsoever, you are practicing along the dhamma.

789
01:06:39,516 --> 01:06:42,098
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, again, you would be developing rightly.

790
01:06:50,327 --> 01:06:51,428
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, thank you very much.

791
01:06:51,888 --> 01:07:03,697
[SPEAKER_00]: Actually, yeah, when the pressure is so strong, I think it constantly, like, avoids me to focus exactly, I mean, to identify the mind.

792
01:07:04,578 --> 01:07:12,284
[SPEAKER_01]: Always go back to the scenario and, you know, it's... Yeah, so basically the pressure is making you focus on things the mind wants you focused.

793
01:07:13,547 --> 01:07:16,608
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, the best a person can do is let me focus on something else.

794
01:07:17,289 --> 01:07:18,149
[SPEAKER_01]: Just focus.

795
01:07:18,169 --> 01:07:19,170
[SPEAKER_01]: Just forget about this.

796
01:07:19,350 --> 01:07:21,971
[SPEAKER_01]: But that does not teach the mind the right thing.

797
01:07:22,071 --> 01:07:24,832
[SPEAKER_01]: So, instead of focusing, unabsorb yourself.

798
01:07:25,292 --> 01:07:30,935
[SPEAKER_01]: When the momentum is trying to get you boiled down to the specifics, don't focus on that.

799
01:07:31,235 --> 01:07:36,517
[SPEAKER_01]: Unfocus yourself from the specifics to, basically, re-feel the state of mind that's already felt.

800
01:07:37,958 --> 01:07:42,280
[SPEAKER_01]: And stay on that level of being unabsorbed to the momentum that's trying to absorb you.

801
01:07:48,394 --> 01:07:48,819
Thank you.

802
01:07:49,748 --> 01:07:50,051
[SPEAKER_01]: Welcome.

